												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Coming Soon To Early Access</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">The developers of this game intend to release as a work in progress, developing with the feedback of players.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Arctic Drive is a major project by a small indie team and it is actively evolving. Early Access allows us to develop the game alongside the community while ensuring the necessary resources to support its growth.<br />
<br />
During this Early Access period we will be creating new content, adding new major features, improving existing systems, hiring additional talent, and expanding our production capacity.<br />
<br />
Early Access also allows us to test the game at scale in real-world conditions. Player feedback helps us identify bugs, balance gameplay systems, improve user experience, and prioritize development efforts.<br />
<br />
Our goal is to build Arctic Drive together with our community. Players who join during Early Access actively contribute to shaping the future of the game.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“We currently expect Arctic Drive to remain in Early Access for approximately a bit under a year.<br />
<br />
This timeframe will allow us to add the major planned features, expand the game’s content, improve performance, and refine the overall experience based on community feedback.<br />
<br />
As with any active development project, this timeline may evolve depending on the needs of the game, player feedback, and new opportunities that arise during development.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Our goal is for the full version of Arctic Drive to be significantly more complete, stable, and content-rich than the Early Access version.<br />
<br />
We plan to introduce new vehicles, new biomes, dynamic events, expanded customization options, additional gameplay mechanics, and a more robust multiplayer experience.<br />
<br />
We will also continue improving performance, optimization, UI/UX, balancing, and overall polish.<br />
<br />
Some major features currently under planning, such as Steam Workshop or other mod support, may also be added during development.<br />
<br />
The roadmap will continue to evolve based on community feedback and insights gathered throughout Early Access.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Arctic Drive is already fully playable and offers a complete core experience focused on exploration, driving, vehicle customization, and multiplayer gameplay.<br />
<br />
However, it is still an actively developed version of the game. Players should expect bugs, balancing issues, incomplete features, placeholder content, and ongoing changes through updates.<br />
<br />
We are continuously working to improve stability and overall quality, but buyers should understand they are joining a project that is still evolving over time.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“Yes. We plan to gradually increase the price as more content, features, and major improvements are added to the game.<br />
<br />
Players who support the game during Early Access benefit from a lower price while also directly contributing to its development.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“The community plays a central role in the development of Arctic Drive.<br />
<br />
We actively monitor feedback, suggestions, and bug reports shared through our Discord server, Steam forums, and other communication channels.<br />
<br />
Community input helps us define priorities, improve existing systems, and guide development decisions.<br />
<br />
We will also share regular updates, patch notes, development insights, and testing phases to keep players informed and involved in the evolution of the game.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
